---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---
<section class="section research-home" id="research">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
        <h2>Security assurance needs <span class="accent-underline">measurable evidence.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-lede">Aegis treats verification as an engineering and research problem: what evidence is sufficient, what an independent verifier can establish, and when a system must refuse to claim more than it knows.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="research-grid">
      <a href="/research#evidence-sufficiency"><article><span class="mono">01</span><h3>Evidence sufficiency</h3><p>What minimum evidence is required before a security-sensitive claim can move from hypothesis to decision?</p><em>Explore research <Icon name="arrow" /></em></article></a>
      <a href="/research#independent-verification"><article><span class="mono">02</span><h3>Independent verification</h3><p>How do we avoid allowing the same system that produced a change to become the sole authority that certifies it?</p><em>Explore research <Icon name="arrow" /></em></article></a>
      <a href="/research#remediation-correctness"><article><span class="mono">03</span><h3>Remediation correctness</h3><p>How do we establish that a patch removed the original security condition without hiding a regression?</p><em>Explore research <Icon name="arrow" /></em></article></a>
      <a href="/research#intent-action"><article><span class="mono">04</span><h3>Intent–action alignment</h3><p>How should a software agent’s requested action be evaluated against the task, permission boundary, and evidence?</p><em>Explore research <Icon name="arrow" /></em></article></a>
    </div>
    <div class="research-footer"><span>Methodology before leaderboard.</span><a class="section-link" href="/research">Open Aegis Research <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.research-home{background:#f8f4ec}.research-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px}.research-grid>a{display:block}.research-grid article{height:100%;min-height:340px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:27px;background:#fffdf8;display:flex;flex-direction:column;transition:transform .22s ease,border-color .22s ease,box-shadow .22s ease}.research-grid a:hover article,.research-grid a:focus-visible article{transform:translateY(-5px);border-color:rgba(169,120,37,.45);box-shadow:0 20px 55px rgba(15,17,21,.08)}.research-grid article>span{color:var(--gold-deep);font-size:9px}.research-grid h3{margin:72px 0 13px;font-size:1.55rem}.research-grid p{color:#4f4c46;font-size:13px;line-height:1.62}.research-grid em{margin-top:auto;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-style:normal;font-weight:820;font-size:11px}.research-grid em svg{width:13px;height:13px}.research-footer{margin-top:27px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;align-items:center}.research-footer>span{color:#5c5953;font:700 10px/1 var(--font-mono);letter-spacing:.05em}.research-footer .section-link{margin-top:0}
@media(max-width:1000px){.research-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}@media(max-width:620px){.research-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.research-grid article{min-height:280px}.research-grid h3{margin-top:50px}.research-footer{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.research-grid article{transition:none}.research-grid a:hover article,.research-grid a:focus-visible article{transform:none}}
</style>
